.env
bin/
*.pem
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# Run output is evidence for whoever ran it, not a committed artefact, with two
# deliberate exceptions. One batch manifest and one full run are tracked so the
# committed table under results/tables/ can be recomputed by anyone: a results
# table with no inputs behind it is a number nobody can check.
#
# Both exceptions are synthetic. The manifest comes out of batch.Generate from a
# seed and the run is the fake layer, so neither carries anything from Razorpay
# and neither is a credential. The live-layer run stays untracked, because its
# order ids are real Razorpay test-mode ids.
#
# The negations need the star form. A rule that excludes the directory itself
# stops git from ever looking inside it, so `results/runs/` with an exception
# under it would not work.
results/runs/*
!results/runs/sample-phase-2-fake/
results/batches/*
!results/batches/b-1234-40.json

# make verify-phase-2 regenerates this pair on every run from the same seeded
# batch as the committed sample, so tracking it would put two identical tables
# in the tree and a diff on every gate run.
results/tables/verify-phase-2.csv
results/tables/verify-phase-2.md
